            <fr:title text="Weekly Review 2026-W30">Weekly Review 2026-W30</fr:title>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter><html:p>This week marked the end of my long reinforcement learning career. I consolidated the current project that we are putting aside in my <fr:link href="/Z902/" title="Idea Purgatory" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/Z902/" display-uri="Z902" type="local">Idea Purgatory</fr:link> for the time being.</html:p><fr:tree show-metadata="false"><fr:frontmatter><fr:authors><fr:author><fr:link href="/kellenkanarios/" title="Kellen Kanarios" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/kellenkanarios/" display-uri="kellenkanarios" type="local">Kellen Kanarios</fr:link></fr:author></fr:authors><fr:date><fr:year>2026</fr:year><fr:month>7</fr:month><fr:day>24</fr:day></fr:date><fr:uri>https://kellenkanarios.com/1AWD/</fr:uri><fr:display-uri>1AWD</fr:display-uri><fr:route>/1AWD/</fr:route><fr:title text="The Quantified Me: 2026-W30"><fr:link href="/G944/" title="The Quantified Me" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/G944/" display-uri="G944" type="local">The Quantified Me</fr:link>: 2026-W30</fr:title></fr:frontmatter><fr:mainmatter><html:p>Another week of note-taking / learning. I wrote a little blog on the <fr:link href="/F3T0/" title="Forward-backward algorithm" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/F3T0/" display-uri="F3T0" type="local">Forward-backward algorithm</fr:link> as part of a long overdo <fr:link href="/005G/" title="Papers of a week" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/005G/" display-uri="005G" type="local">POTW</fr:link> on <fr:link href="/ZUAG/" title="POTW: Multi-Level Discovery of Deep Options" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/ZUAG/" display-uri="ZUAG" type="local">DDO</fr:link>. Also did a brief write-up on <fr:link href="/G27U/" title="POTW: Learning Options via Compression" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/G27U/" display-uri="G27U" type="local">LOVE</fr:link> that I might come back to at some point.</html:p><html:figure><html:img width="100%" src="/bafkrmihchehyd5enjoe7oguy5ajjluvgbxneneb7eq3swsob7purv7423i.png" />
  <html:figcaption>Coding hours for week 2026-W30.</html:figcaption></html:figure><html:p>It seems like brain-rotting is no longer a problem for me. I do not have any social media accounts remaining so there is not much for me to watch. The study time is down bit because I have done a poor job expanding my Anki deck but a great job staying on top of it.</html:p><html:figure><html:img width="100%" src="/bafkrmifv4q3vwyb4b3hhlmqxvvjyabajsw7r2kmcjiqxzc5a4rq5djigpy.png" />
  <html:figcaption>Non-coding computer time for week 2026-W30.</html:figcaption></html:figure></fr:mainmatter></fr:tree><fr:tree show-metadata="false"><fr:frontmatter><fr:authors><fr:author><fr:link href="/kellenkanarios/" title="Kellen Kanarios" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/kellenkanarios/" display-uri="kellenkanarios" type="local">Kellen Kanarios</fr:link></fr:author></fr:authors><fr:date><fr:year>2026</fr:year><fr:month>7</fr:month><fr:day>24</fr:day></fr:date><fr:uri>https://kellenkanarios.com/43BK/</fr:uri><fr:display-uri>43BK</fr:display-uri><fr:route>/43BK/</fr:route><fr:title text="Life Maxing: 2026-W30"><fr:link href="/5501/" title="Life Maxing" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/5501/" display-uri="5501" type="local">Life Maxing</fr:link>: 2026-W30</fr:title></fr:frontmatter><fr:mainmatter><html:p>The running numbers are a little misleading because the missed runs last week due to the fires actually ended up on this week. On my Garmin cycle, I got to 40 miles, so we are back up to where we need to be. However, due to my illness, my VO2 max has crashed. Need to get that back up ASAP.</html:p><html:figure><html:img width="100%" src="/bafkrmiepvsbpzwaugfiq5xfm4izczybcholig2csssfzdp6i7eqp3xpukm.png" />
  <html:figcaption>Health stats for week 2026-W30.</html:figcaption></html:figure><html:p>Friday night I went to Detroit and it carried over into Saturday, which was then my Moms birthday. It seems that Leetcode is my biggest contextual-dependent habit i.e. I do not do it consistently when I am out of routine. I hope to dial this back in even though I will be out of town next week (do not like my odds).</html:p></fr:mainmatter></fr:tree><fr:tree show-metadata="false"><fr:frontmatter><fr:authors><fr:author><fr:link href="/kellenkanarios/" title="Kellen Kanarios" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/kellenkanarios/" display-uri="kellenkanarios" type="local">Kellen Kanarios</fr:link></fr:author></fr:authors><fr:date><fr:year>2026</fr:year><fr:month>7</fr:month><fr:day>24</fr:day></fr:date><fr:uri>https://kellenkanarios.com/GW1X/</fr:uri><fr:display-uri>GW1X</fr:display-uri><fr:route>/GW1X/</fr:route><fr:title text="Reading Corner: 2026-W30"><fr:link href="/RPP0/" title="Reading Corner" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/RPP0/" display-uri="RPP0" type="local">Reading Corner</fr:link>: 2026-W30</fr:title></fr:frontmatter><fr:mainmatter><html:p>A long week of reading. I am still working my way through <fr:link href="/hofstadterGodelEscherBach1999/" title="Gödel, Escher, Bach: An Eternal Goden Braid" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/hofstadterGodelEscherBach1999/" display-uri="hofstadterGodelEscherBach1999" type="local">GEB</fr:link>, but it has become significantly more dense as we get to more formal mathematics. I will be starting <fr:link href="/macintyreSpyTraitorIncredible2018/" title="The Spy and the Traitor: An incredible espionage and spy thriller and the greatest true story of the Cold War" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/macintyreSpyTraitorIncredible2018/" display-uri="macintyreSpyTraitorIncredible2018" type="local">The Spy and the Traitor: An incredible espionage and spy thriller and the greatest true story of the Cold War</fr:link>.</html:p><fr:tree show-metadata="false"><fr:frontmatter><fr:authors><fr:author><fr:link href="/kellenkanarios/" title="Kellen Kanarios" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/kellenkanarios/" display-uri="kellenkanarios" type="local">Kellen Kanarios</fr:link></fr:author></fr:authors><fr:date><fr:year>2026</fr:year><fr:month>7</fr:month><fr:day>28</fr:day></fr:date><fr:uri>https://kellenkanarios.com/4SOC/</fr:uri><fr:display-uri>4SOC</fr:display-uri><fr:route>/4SOC/</fr:route><fr:title text="Review: Candide">Review: <fr:link href="/voltaireCandide2015/" title="Candide" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/voltaireCandide2015/" display-uri="voltaireCandide2015" type="local">Candide</fr:link></fr:title></fr:frontmatter><fr:mainmatter><html:p>I did very little research prior to reading this book and was not at all aware of what I was getting into. It turns out this book is quite the controversial piece of philosophy. For what was supposed to be a light read, I ended up deep in the weeds on the meaning of life and flaws of humanity. The book is basically a stance against the idea of blind optimisim and the notion that <html:em>everything is as it should be</html:em>. More importantly, even if this were the case (in El Dorado) the human condition would not allow us to simply sit idle in such a place. However, I actually found the conclusion highly inspiring.  <html:em>Cultivate your garden</html:em> - life will not</html:p><html:p>For what it is, I think it is a 7/10.</html:p><html:figure><html:img width="50%" src="/bafkrmica2bnzujxbtqb4phuykwp3j3er55nvara4quzwb5s3hpdbpg4e3q.jpg" />
<html:figcaption /></html:figure></fr:mainmatter></fr:tree><fr:tree show-metadata="false"><fr:frontmatter><fr:authors><fr:author><fr:link href="/kellenkanarios/" title="Kellen Kanarios" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/kellenkanarios/" display-uri="kellenkanarios" type="local">Kellen Kanarios</fr:link></fr:author></fr:authors><fr:date><fr:year>2026</fr:year><fr:month>7</fr:month><fr:day>28</fr:day></fr:date><fr:uri>https://kellenkanarios.com/2I8C/</fr:uri><fr:display-uri>2I8C</fr:display-uri><fr:route>/2I8C/</fr:route><fr:title text="Review: Elon Musk">Review: <fr:link href="/isaacsonElonMusk2023/" title="Elon Musk" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/isaacsonElonMusk2023/" display-uri="isaacsonElonMusk2023" type="local">Elon Musk</fr:link></fr:title></fr:frontmatter><fr:mainmatter><html:p>If nothing else, this book made me realize I need to work harder. I am not sure that daddy issues is a sufficient explanation for some of Musk's highly erratic actions. However, it is indisputable the drive and work ethic he both has and demands from his companies. I often wonder whether a relentless tyrant like Musk could maximize my potential, but it is very apparent here that it would come at a severe cost. Getting back to the book, I think it felt a little propaganda-y. I find it hard to believe Elon is a pure intentioned savior of humanity. Though, I do not doubt he likes to seem himself that way.</html:p><html:p>Twitter part was too long, 5/10.</html:p><html:figure><html:img width="50%" src="/bafkrmiaitjlkmko7bpcdfzqvvlqpnz6imaldkal5azxo5uag4fjjtwkjwy.jpg" />
<html:figcaption>Elon aura-farming too hard (we all saw the Ari yacht photo).</html:figcaption></html:figure></fr:mainmatter></fr:tree></fr:mainmatter></fr:tree>
